<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Associated Domains for Universal Links (email confirmation opening the native app).

  Wired into Debug and Release via CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS in project.pbxproj.
  Associated Domains is enabled on App ID com.treforged.forged and the "Forged App Store"
  provisioning profile was regenerated with it on 2026-07-27. Release signs Manual against
  that pinned profile, so the BUILD_PROVISION_PROFILE_BASE64 GitHub secret must carry the
  REGENERATED profile or the iOS build will fail at signing.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:getforgenta.com</string>
	</array>

	<!--
	  APNs. WITHOUT THIS KEY iOS PUSH CANNOT WORK AT ALL, and it was missing until 2026-09-05.

	  `PushNotifications.register()` fails with a `registrationError` and no token is ever minted,
	  which is exactly what the data showed: `device_tokens` held 7 rows, every one ANDROID, and
	  ZERO iOS — while `APNS_AUTH_KEY_P8`, `APNS_KEY_ID` and `APNS_TEAM_ID` all sat correctly
	  configured in Supabase. A perfect `.p8` signs nothing for an app the OS will not register.

	  ⚠️ THE VALUE IS `production`, AND `development` WAS WRONG — I WROTE IT, WITH A CONFIDENT AND
	  INCORRECT JUSTIFICATION, IN `c1cff973`. That comment claimed "development covers debug and
	  TestFlight builds; the App Store submission rewrites it to production when Apple re-signs."
	  It does not. **A TestFlight build is DISTRIBUTION-signed and registers against the PRODUCTION
	  APNs environment.** With `development`, iOS asks the sandbox for a token on a build that is
	  not entitled to one, and `register()` is accepted and then never calls back.

	  That is exactly what it did: 22 registration attempts from Tre's iPhone between 17:33Z and
	  18:33Z, every one recorded `timeout` with `prompted: false` — permission granted, the OS
	  simply never answering. The entitlement was present and had the wrong value, which is a
	  failure that looks identical to the entitlement being absent.

	  `production` is correct for every build this repo produces: `ios-build.yml` only ever archives
	  `-configuration Release` and exports `app-store-connect`. A local Xcode debug build is the one
	  case that would want `development`, and nothing in CI makes one.

	  ⚠️ THIS KEY ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH, AND IT BREAKS SIGNING UNTIL THE OTHER HALF IS DONE.
	  Release signs Manual against the pinned "Forged App Store" profile (see the note above), so
	  a profile without the Push Notifications capability will FAIL at the signing step rather
	  than build something that quietly cannot register. That is the better failure — loud instead
	  of silent — but it does mean these three steps must happen in the Apple Developer portal:
	    1. Enable Push Notifications on App ID `com.treforged.forged`.
	    2. Regenerate the "Forged App Store" provisioning profile so it carries the capability.
	    3. Re-encode it into the `BUILD_PROVISION_PROFILE_BASE64` GitHub secret.
	  Only Tre can do those; nothing in this repo can.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
